; UI-PAD1. `ui_accept` is a Godot built-in and was NOT listed here, so the
; engine defaults applied -- and those defaults, in this project, carried no
; joypad event at all. Dumped from the live InputMap before this change:
;
;   ui_accept     -> key, key, key      <- nothing a controller can press
;   ui_left       -> key, JOY:13, axis:0
;   menu_confirm  -> key, JOY:0
;
; A Godot `Button` activates on `ui_accept`. So focus NAVIGATION worked on a
; pad and focus ACCEPT did not: every Button-driven screen in a controller-first
; game could be walked around and never pressed. Verified on the build menu with
; real InputEventJoypadButton presses -- focus sat on a grid cell and neither A
; nor X armed a piece.
;
; Listing the action here REPLACES the engine defaults rather than adding to
; them, so the three keyboard events are restated deliberately. Dropping any of
; them would silently take Enter or Space away from every menu in the game;
; `tests/test_controls.gd::test_ui_accept_still_answers_the_keyboard` exists to
; catch exactly that.
;
; Sharing joypad A with `menu_confirm` is intentional, not a collision. Enter
; has always been both on the keyboard, so every screen that polls
; `menu_confirm` has already been living with this pairing -- see that test
; file's own note, and `ralph/NOTES.md`.
ui_accept={
"deadzone": 0.5,
"events": [Object(InputEventKey,"device":-1,"keycode":4194309,"pressed":false,"script":null)
, Object(InputEventKey,"device":-1,"keycode":4194310,"pressed":false,"script":null)
, Object(InputEventKey,"device":-1,"keycode":32,"pressed":false,"script":null)
, Object(InputEventJoypadButton,"device":-1,"button_index":0,"pressed":false,"script":null)
]
}
menu_confirm={
"deadzone": 0.5,
"events": [Object(InputEventKey,"device":-1,"physical_keycode":4194309,"pressed":false,"script":null)
, Object(InputEventJoypadButton,"device":-1,"button_index":0,"pressed":false,"script":null)
]
}
